# CQ 09: Which data is recorded, and where?
#
# Where data comes from is two steps away: the acquisition names the source it
# was taken from, and the assignment names the device carrying out that
# acquisition.
#
# Source and device answer different questions. The source says what the data
# is about, the device says where in the plant it was taken. The two often
# nearly coincide, but they need not: an acquisition running on an edge device
# may well read a sensor two levels below.
#
# Anchored on the data rather than on the production data. What an acquisition
# yields is not always typed as production data: in case 2 the three
# acquisitions deliver plain data, and only the result of merging them is
# production data. Asking for the narrower class would have missed all three.
PREFIX aias:     <https://w3id.org/aias#>
PREFIX vdi3682:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#>
PREFIX iso22989: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
PREFIX rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?data ?dataKind ?acquisition ?source ?resource
WHERE {
  ?data iso22989:isAcquiredBy ?acquisition .
  ?data a ?dataKind . ?dataKind rdfs:subClassOf* iso22989:Data .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?data a ?n . ?n rdfs:subClassOf+ ?dataKind }
  OPTIONAL { ?acquisition iso22989:hasDataSource ?source }
  OPTIONAL { ?acquisition aias:isAssignedTo/vdi3682:isAssignedTo ?resource }
} ORDER BY ?data
